#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092995} :activity/id #uuid "95d8fd9f-fddb-5a11-8670-194ad28cdab0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049392 :topic/id #uuid "f1031f6b-01e9-5ea8-af71-27bacc9d53b8" :topic/math-academy-id 1023} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092995 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093403 :tutorial/content "We know that we can write a system of three linear equations in three variables in the form $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n- $A$ is the $3\\times 3$ coefficient matrix,\n\n- $\\mathbf{x}$ is the column vector of variables, and\n\n- $\\mathbf{b}$ is the column vector of constants.\n\nIf the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ is invertible, then we can find a solution to the system $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ by \"pre-multiplying\" both sides of the equation by $A^{-1}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ {A}^{-1}Ax & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ {I}_{3}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the solution of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b},$ we simply calculate $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nLet's see how this works for a particular system in the next example." :tutorial/id #uuid "4c0fe954-2cf5-5eb6-b58f-c6963f5be7f2" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3054 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "8e9e60d9-ca5d-5380-9aad-e2eb767f920e" :step/math-academy-id 16484 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092996}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092996 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092185 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092025 :question/id #uuid "2737e6bc-5372-50a0-bf2f-59a91f571a57" :question/math-academy-id "e-4520"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049151} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050825}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092817} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092818} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292892} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348080} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348093} {:db/i